  "title": "Null, empty or blank",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Problem statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "text": "`null` is no String at all, `\"\"` is an empty String, and `\"   \"` is a blank one: not empty, but only whitespace. `isEmpty()` and `isBlank()` tell the last two apart, and neither can be called on `null`, which is checked first."
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "text": "Write `kind(String s)` in `Kinds`. It returns:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "s",
        "result"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`null`",
          "`\"null\"`"
        ],
        [
          "`\"\"`",
          "`\"empty\"`"
        ],
        [
          "`\"   \"`, `\"\\t\\n\"`",
          "`\"blank\"`"
        ],
        [
          "`\"hi\"`, `\" hi \"`",
          "`\"text\"`"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Lesson"
    },
    {
      "type": "disclosure",
      "summary": "Show a worked solution",
      "open": false,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "text": "package practice;\n\npublic final class Kinds {\n\n    private Kinds() {\n    }\n\n    /** Says whether s is null, empty, blank or text. */\n    public static String kind(String s) {\n        if (s == null) {\n            return \"null\";\n        }\n        if (s.isEmpty()) {\n            return \"empty\";\n        }\n        if (s.isBlank()) {\n            return \"blank\";\n        }\n        return \"text\";\n    }\n}\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
